isk"], "rationale": "Klobuchar leads the recent polling by seven to ten points, holds an overwhelming money advantage, and both rating outlets and betting markets treat her as a strong favorite in an open D+3 seat. The $10 million outside buy for Demuth and her small-town appeal in greater Minnesota are real but unlikely to erase a deficit this size against a candidate with Klobuchar's name recognition.", "watch": "Whether the Demuth-aligned PAC's $10 million advertising campaign and the fall televised debates close the seven-to-ten-point gap the polls currently show.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open with Tim Walz retiring, and Democrats have turned to Senator Amy Klobuchar, one of the state's best-known politicians, against Republican House leader Lisa Demuth. Polls since mid-September show Klobuchar ahead by seven to ten points, with only a Republican-sponsored survey finding a two-point race. Rating outlets line up between Likely and Solid Democratic, and betting markets put Democratic odds above ninety percent.\n\nKlobuchar has raised roughly twenty times more than Demuth and holds a large cash advantage, though a Demuth-aligned committee recently received a $10 million infusion to fund advertising. Demuth, a St. Cloud-area legislator, has broken with Washington on the Iran war and is courting greater Minnesota, where her small-town profile may help. The state's three-point Democratic lean and Klobuchar's long record of statewide wins frame the race, but the open seat and heavy outside spending leave some room for movement.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}]}